option.autoMinimize=Minimize on lost focus
option.autoMinimize.tooltip=Requires exclusive fullscreen mode
option.fullscreenResolution=Fullscreen Resolution
option.fullscreenResolution.tooltip=Changes the actual display mode of the monitor. Using a custom Fullscreen Resolution will disable Borderless Fullscreen and override the Render Resolution
option.fullscreenResolution.default=Default
option.renderResolution=Render Resolution
option.renderResolution.tooltip=Renders the game at a custom resolution and stretches it to fill the window. The monitor stays at its own resolution, so this works with Borderless Fullscreen
option.renderResolutionKeepAspectRatio=Keep Aspect Ratio
option.renderResolutionKeepAspectRatio.tooltip=Fits the image inside the window instead of stretching it, so a resolution with a different aspect ratio is not distorted. Leaves black bars on two sides
option.renderResolutionSharpScaling=Sharp Scaling
option.renderResolutionSharpScaling.tooltip=Scales the image without smoothing it, which keeps pixel edges crisp instead of blurry. Looks best when the render resolution divides evenly into the window size
option.guiResolution=GUI Resolution
option.guiResolution.tooltip=Places the gui and the hud as if the window had this resolution, while the game keeps rendering at the real one. Fixes a hud that was set up at a different resolution without making anything blurry. Leave the Render Resolution on Default when using this
option.guiResolutionKeepAspectRatio=GUI Keep Aspect Ratio
option.guiResolutionKeepAspectRatio.tooltip=Scales the gui evenly instead of stretching it to the shape of the window, so nothing is distorted. Element sizes stay right but positions along the wider axis no longer match exactly
option.guiResolutionHudOnly=GUI Resolution: HUD Only
option.guiResolutionHudOnly.tooltip=Applies the GUI Resolution only while no screen is open, so menus are laid out and drawn exactly as they are without the mod. The hud moves back to the normal size for as long as a screen is open, including chat
option.guiResolutionCursorSpace=GUI Resolution: Move Cursor With GUI
option.guiResolutionCursorSpace.tooltip=Reports cursor positions in the GUI Resolution instead of the real window. Turn this on while dragging a hud from another mod into place, if the hud runs away from the pointer, and off again afterwards. Leave it off otherwise: anything drawing outside the normal gui, such as a NanoVG based menu, needs the real positions and is thrown off by the same amount in the other direction
option.guiResolutionNormalCrosshair=GUI Resolution: Normal Crosshair
option.guiResolutionNormalCrosshair.tooltip=Draws the crosshair and the attack indicator at the shape they have without a GUI Resolution. A stretched GUI Resolution makes a gui unit wider than it is tall, which is wanted for anything laid out in those units but not for a square in the middle of the screen
option.startInFullscreen=Start in Fullscreen
option.startInFullscreen.tooltip=When disabled, the game will always start in windowed mode
option.replaceVideoSettings=Replace Fullscreen Button
option.replaceVideoSettings.tooltip=Changes the fullscreen button in the video settings menu to contain a borderless option
option.captureCursorInFullscreen=Capture Cursor
option.captureCursorInFullscreen.tooltip=Captures the cursor and prevents it from being moved onto another monitor when in fullscreen
option.configScreenHotkeyEnabled=Config Screen Hotkey
option.configScreenHotkeyEnabled.tooltip=When enabled, the config screen can be opened by pressing CTRL and the fullscreen key. The config screen can also be opened with the "Mod Menu" mod
option.logCoordinates=Log Coordinates
option.logCoordinates.tooltip=Writes the sizes the game is working with to the log whenever they change, including the two ratios that have to agree for clicking to land where the gui is drawn. Only useful when something ends up in the wrong place

